    {
      "description": "The well-being thresholds in this dataset are different to the standard well-being thresholds that are published as part of this release. This is because the data for the anxiety measure needs to be interpreted differently to the other three well-being measures. For example, high happiness scores relate to a positive well-being, while high anxiety scores relate to a poor well-being.\n\nThe well-being thresholds used in this dataset map onto the thresholds used in the main publication in the following way:\n\n- Poor = Low levels of life satisfaction, worthwhile, happiness and high levels of anxiety.\n- Fair = Medium levels of life satisfaction, worthwhile, happiness and anxiety.\n- Good = High levels of life satisfaction, worthwhile, happiness and low levels of anxiety.\n- Very good = Very high levels of life satisfaction, worthwhile, happiness and very low levels of anxiety.",
